<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#SemioticProjection> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Semiotic Projection is about the projection of the User seeing the meme onto a certain part of the meme. The projection could be onto some VisualMaterial or some TextualMaterial or some Scene."@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01247#racism> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#relatedTo> <http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01247#text_chunk> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01247#racist_joke_scene> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The scene features a black-and-white portrait of Adolf Hitler, who is the central visual entity. He is depicted looking directly at the camera with a stern expression, wearing a military-style uniform with a strap over his shoulder. Overlaid on the image is text that reads 'you can't be racist if there is no other race', which creates a juxtaposition between the historical figure's association with racism and the ironic or satirical statement. The scene is composed to provoke thought or humor by combining a symbol of extreme racism with a logically absurd statement."@en .
