<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01247#mapping_1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The textual material 'you can't be racist if there is no other race' is juxtaposed with the visual material of Adolf Hitler, who is the historical embodiment of racist ideology. The mapping is that the text's ironic statement about racism is being projected onto Hitler, using his visual representation as a symbol of extreme racism to highlight the absurdity of the claim. This is an analogical mapping where the text's concept is mapped onto the visual entity representing the extreme manifestation of that concept."@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#contradicts> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Indicates contradictory relationship between dimension instances"@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01247#mapping_1> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#extractionMethod> "llm_extraction_huggingface" .
