<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01247#dimension_1> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#extractionMethod> "regex_fallback" .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#Value> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "One dimension embodying certain values versus another dimension embodying opposing values in memes, e.g. text and visuals representing conflicting moral or aesthetic values"@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01247#satire> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A literary, dramatic, or artistic work that uses humor, irony, exaggeration, or ridicule to criticize and expose the absurdities or vices of individuals, institutions, or society. The meme is a form of satire that critiques racism by using a shocking juxtaposition to make a point about the nature of prejudice."@en .
